app_tool_definitions.description:
Authority-gated Bonfÿre institutional operating system for native tools, work, evidence, finance, CMS, and Matrix operations.

Run isolated plan, implementation, review, conditional repair, tests and concurrent independent final verification. Apply candidates are checked before reviews. Failed tests get one bounded repair in the same worktree, then persistent failure stops verification. Optional apply uses current Project policy and preimage checks. Optional source_files capture selected current files by SHA-256 into the isolated baseline. Invalid or stale inputs stop before model calls; the final patch excludes baseline inputs. This does not relax Project write policy. This tool is part of plugin `AurekaiBonfyre`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__aurekaibonfyre_implementation_relay(args: {
  apply_to_project?: boolean;
  prompt: string;
  // Optional explicit current-source coverage over the configured Git base. Supply whole-file SHA-256 from project_read; null requires absence. Up to 8 MiB total. Unselected paths stay at the Git base. Ignored files and symlinks are refused.
  source_files?: Array<{ path: string; sha256: string | null; }>;
  title?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Authority-gated Bonfÿre institutional operating system for native tools, work, evidence, finance, CMS, and Matrix operations.

Find native owners by family, capability or synopsis. Prefer query plus detail=summary for routing; use full details only for selected matches. Empty arguments preserve the full legacy inventory. Discovery does not prove runtime readiness. This tool is part of plugin `AurekaiBonfyre`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__aurekaibonfyre_native_tool_inventory(args: {
  detail?: "summary" | "full";
  // Defaults to 20 when any filter or display option is supplied.
  limit?: number;
  offset?: number;
  query?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Authority-gated Bonfÿre institutional operating system for native tools, work, evidence, finance, CMS, and Matrix operations.

Read one source range or up to 16 file ranges in one call, with exact whole-file SHA-256 and continuation lines. Use files for related owners/tests. if_sha256 returns only identity when unchanged. Shared batch limits: 32 MiB source, 512 KiB response. File reads are individually checked, not an atomic checkout snapshot. This tool is part of plugin `AurekaiBonfyre`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__aurekaibonfyre_project_read(args: {
  end_line?: number;
  // Use instead of top-level path and range options.
  files?: Array<{
  end_line?: number;
  // Previously observed whole-file digest. Matching bytes omit content; this does not attest prior range coverage.
  if_sha256?: string;
  path: string;
  start_line?: number;
}>;
  // Previously observed whole-file digest. Matching bytes omit content; this does not attest prior range coverage.
  if_sha256?: string;
  path?: string;
  start_line?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```
